		{
			"id": "eMn1QRTBuT8gYdY7x",
			"description": "Choppa",
			"local_notes": "Ork blades are all edge and mass, not balance; a choppa is never \"sharp\" in the fine sense, but a Boy's own strength does the real work.\n\nLore: The choppa is the other half of every Boy's standard loadout alongside the slugga: a heavy, crudely-forged cleaver, machete or cut-down sword welded from scrap and scavenged plate, and the single most common Ork melee weapon in Codex: Orks background, Deathwatch's Mark of the Xenos, and every piece of Ork army art the game has ever produced.\n\nDesign: Matches the framework's Ork anchor exactly (\"Choppa | Crude cleaver, sw+3 cut, parry -1U\"). At a Boy's own ST 22 (sw approx. 3d+2) this averages roughly sw+3=3d+5, comparable in raw power to an Imperium chainsword in Astartes hands despite having no motor or armour divisor at all - the framework's own point that Ork weapons \"compensate for crude construction with a Boy's raw strength,\" not with mechanism. Handling: weight 10 lb, heavier than any human-scale cutting weapon on this project's Imperium melee page (the Chainaxe, at 15 lb, is the closest comparison) for the crude, over-thick, badly-balanced blade every choppa depiction shows; min ST 11 (a real, if rough, forged blade this heavy needs genuine strength to swing with any control) is trivial for a Boy and out of easy reach for an unaugmented human, matching the constant depiction of looted choppas being unwieldy in human hands. Skill Axe/Mace and parry -1U, per the anchor directly and consistent with every other heavy chopping weapon on the project's Imperium melee page (the Chainaxe, Power Axe, etc.).",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Orks"
			],
