		{
			"id": "ee0pTiPLbzZ9a7jnW",
			"description": "Big Choppa",
			"local_notes": "A big two-handed cleaver, often favoured by Nobz who forgo a shield hand.\n\nLore: A two-handed, oversized choppa favoured by Nobz and mob bosses who want more reach and more raw hitting power than a one-handed choppa without going as far as a power klaw; a recurring silhouette in Codex: Orks Nob artwork and background, distinguished from the standard choppa mainly by size and the two-handed grip.\n\nDesign: One step up the same Basic Set two-handed-weapon-over-one-handed relationship this project uses elsewhere (the Imperium Eviscerator over the Chainaxe, or the Thunder Hammer's two-handed grip over a one-handed power maul): +1 die over the Choppa anchor's sw+3 cut, giving sw+4 cut, two-handed, reach 1,2. At a Nob's own ST 26 (sw approx. 4d+1) this averages roughly 4d+5 - a genuinely brutal blow against unarmoured or lightly-armoured targets, with no armour divisor and (checked by exact dice distribution) 0% against flak (DR 30) or better, keeping it - like the plain choppa - a horde and infantry weapon rather than a threat to real armour, exactly the niche a mundane, unpowered Ork blade should occupy relative to the power klaw below. Handling: weight 18 lb (heavier than the one-handed choppa's 10 lb for the bigger blade and two-handed haft), min ST 15 (comfortable for a Nob, a real stretch for a Boy, unreachable for an unaugmented human), Two-Handed Axe/Mace skill and parry -1U matching the same convention as every heavy chopping weapon on this and the Imperium melee page.",
