		{
			"id": "eUKjB-yzNLFnqQr1k",
			"description": "Killsaw",
			"local_notes": "Cannot be used to Feint, as the Imperium Power Fist and Chainfist it's built from. Like the power klaw, the ring of chain-teeth carries a genuine (if crudely copied and worse-shielded) disruption field behind its spinning edge - Ork background is explicit that a killsaw bites through vehicle hulls and bulkheads the way a plain chain weapon never could, and this project models that with the same Armor Divisor every disruption-field weapon in this project shares, not with a bigger mundane blade. The teeth can still bind in a very solid hit exactly as an Imperium chainaxe's can (GM's discretion: a Ready maneuver to wrench it free).\n\nLore: A huge, motorised chain-blade mounted on a Meganob's arm alongside (or instead of) a power klaw, built for boarding actions and breaching where cutting through plate matters; Codex: Orks background places it as the Ork parallel to the Imperium chainfist, and is explicit that it genuinely cuts into tank hulls and bulkheads in the field - not merely a bigger version of a Boy-scale choppa's chain-teeth.\n\nDesign: REVISED (lore fix): the previous build treated the killsaw as a mundane grinding-chain mechanism on the Imperium Chainaxe/Chainfist model with its own Armor Divisor (3), which left it unable to hurt power armour or a vehicle in any reliable way (0.1% vs Astartes plate, effectively 0% vs every vehicle AV) - directly contradicted by Ork background's own claim that a killsaw cuts through tank hulls and bulkheads. Rebuilt instead exactly on the Imperium Power Fist/Chainfist chassis the coordinator specified: thr+7d(10) cut, the Chainfist's own formula (see data/imperium/weapons/melee.yaml), reasoned here as a crude, worse-shielded disruption field a Mek has copied or looted into the chain housing rather than a plain mechanical grind - \"cruder\" is carried in cost, upkeep and the entry's own tone, not a weaker divisor, exactly the same design choice this file already makes for the Power Klaw relative to the Imperium Power Fist. Checked by exact dice distribution at the mega-armour-assisted strength a Meganob fights at (effective thrust around thr 3d+1, so thr+7d = 10d+1): avg 36, penetrating every personal armour on the table at or above 99.9%, including a Terminator, and clearing AV10-12 essentially always, AV13 94.2% of the time and even AV14 53.6% of the time - reaching (and, at a Meganob's own greater bulk, slightly exceeding) the Astartes Chainfist's own benchmark figures, exactly the \"must reach chainfist-level armour penetration\" the coordinator asked for, and finally matching the fiction's own claim that killsaws open up tank hulls and bulkheads rather than merely chewing infantry. Handling: weight up from 40 lb to 42 lb and cost up sharply (a genuine field-bearing weapon, not a plain motorised blade, costs and weighs accordingly, in line with the Power Klaw's own price jump over a mundane chain weapon); reach C, parry -2 and the no-Feint note are taken directly from the Imperium Power Fist/Chainfist, since a fist-and-forearm-mounted spinning chain ring fights exactly like a servo-driven punching weapon, not a swung two-handed blade - this also corrects the skill to Brawling (unarmed-style, arm-mounted) in place of the previous Two-Handed Axe/Mace, matching how the Imperium Chainfist itself is built despite sharing a name with the swung Chainaxe. Min ST 22, reachable by mega armour's own servo assistance or an unusually huge Ork, per the notes.",
