		{
			"id": "eiTz3ARSTlpLKR8HB",
			"description": "Power Stabba",
			"local_notes": "Field toggle as the Imperium Power Sword family; a depleted or crudely-wired cell disables the field the same way.\n\nLore: A rarer, thrusting cousin of the power klaw - a heavy iron stake or spike wrapped in the same crude field generator - favoured by Nobz who want to punch through a target rather than crush it; less iconic than the power klaw but recurring in Ork background as an alternative Nob power weapon.\n\nDesign: Applies this project's power-field rule (framework.md: +3d damage, Armor Divisor (10), field on vs. off) to a plain heavy iron stake's mundane baseline (thr+2 imp, one step above a bare thrusting spike for the sheer mass of Ork ironwork) rather than to the power klaw's own crushing baseline, since a stabbing spike and a crushing gauntlet are not the same mundane weapon with a field bolted on. Checked by exact dice distribution at a Nob's own strength (thr approx. 2d+1, so field on totals thr+2+3d = 5d+3): avg 20.5, penetrating every personal armour at or above 99.7% up to Astartes power armour, and 50.0% of the time even against a Terminator - a genuinely dangerous power weapon in a Nob's hands, on the same tier as the Imperium's own human-scale Power Sword against comparable armour, matching its place as a real but secondary alternative to the power klaw. Handling: 20 lb (lighter than the Power Klaw's 45 lb - a spike and generator, not a full gauntlet), min ST 18 (a Nob manages it readily; a Boy struggles), Spear skill and reach 1 for a thrusting weapon, parry -1U matching the Imperium Power Lance's own crude, hard-to-recover braced-spear convention.",
