		{
			"id": "eiT4KQE25XduA8gX_",
			"description": "Grabba Stikk",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A long hooked pole Ork mobs use to drag fleeing enemies back into reach, pull a wounded comrade clear, or hook a Grot by the collar; a recurring, unglamorous piece of Ork kit in background art rather than a named weapon of note, more tool than trophy.\n\nDesign: Not anchored by the framework; built from Basic Set polearm design logic as a plain, long-hafted hooked pole (sw+1 cr, reach 1,2, parry 0, per a standard polearm's Basic Set baseline) with the hook's real function - grappling rather than damage - called out as a GM-run option rather than a bespoke mechanic, since GURPS already has grappling rules this project prefers to reuse over inventing a new one. Handling: 12 lb for a long wooden or scrap-metal pole with an iron hook, min ST 10 (light work for any Ork, a real if manageable weapon for a strong human).",
			"tags": [
				"Melee Weapon",
				"Xenos",
				"Orks"
			],
