		{
			"id": "e0FsWLTRkoc8WYVTU",
			"description": "'Urty Syringe",
			"local_notes": "Lore: A Painboy's oversized hypodermic, as often used to \"fix\" a patient as to threaten one into holding still for surgery; Codex: Orks background treats Painboyz' medical practice as simultaneously legitimate battlefield surgery (by Ork standards, which include successfully reattaching severed limbs and heads) and a source of constant dread for anyone made to sit still for it, the 'urty syringe being the visual shorthand for both.\n\nDesign: Not anchored; built as a short, thrust-only stabbing weapon on the Basic Set Knife profile (thr-1 imp, reach C, parry -1, matching the Imperium Munitorum Combat Knife's own corrected parry) with a tox follow-up standing in for whatever crude injection the needle actually delivers, left deliberately unspecified (per Ork medical background's own black humour) rather than statted as a single fixed poison. Handling: 2 lb, a hand-held hypodermic tool rather than a combat blade; min ST 8, trivial for any Ork, in reach of an unaugmented human too, since this is fundamentally a tool that sometimes doubles as a weapon rather than the other way around.",
